KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--winx64 --cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ setw: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ setprecision: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ setbase: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ setiosflags: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ resetiosflags: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The manipulators had no model: the _Smanip they returned held an unknown
function pointer, so inserting one called through an invalid pointer (and
the MSVC STL's `ss << setw(4)' dispatched to every function of a
compatible type, cpp11_stream_setw timing out).
